==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|finstar}}, which probably dissimilated from {{m|goh|dinstar}}, making it a descendant of {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þiustrijaz||dark, without light}}. See also Dutch [[duister]] and German [[düster]].

